# the reasoning.
#
# Empty rather than a path. With no --ffmpeg argument on the command line
# Jellyfin falls through to <EncoderAppPath> in /etc/jellyfin/encoding.xml, which
# leaves exactly one place that names the encoder and keeps the dashboard's
# "FFmpeg path" field working. A path written here would outrank both of those
# and an operator changing the field would see no effect.
#
# A separate file, rather than an edit to /etc/default/jellyfin, because that one
# is a dpkg conffile: rewriting it makes every jellyfin-server upgrade a conffile
# conflict that apt resolves by prompting or by keeping a stale copy.
